er=false, source=\"input_text\".\n- If a duration is NOT mentioned, do NOT invent a realistic value. Use exactly:\n  distribution=\"fixed\", value=1.0, unit=\"minutes\", is_placeholder=true, source=\"default_missing_duration\".\n- Apply this rule to every task duration AND to inter_arrival_time.\n- Never invent branch probabilities: include branch_probabilities only if stated in the text; otherwise leave them null and put the decision labels (e.g. \"igen\"/\"nem\") into branch_conditions and the sequence-flow condition_name.\n\nStructural correctness (CRITICAL):\n- Every task and gateway MUST have at least one outgoing and one incoming sequence_flow (unless adjacent to a start/end event).\n- All sequence_flow source_id and target_id values MUST reference existing element IDs.\n- Do NOT leave dead ends or orphans.\n\nPools and message flows (IMPORTANT - do not skip):\n- Whenever the text names two or more distinct organisational units, departments, workshops, roles, or locations that hand work, documents, or material to each other, you MUST model each as a separate pool, and list every element that belongs to it in element_ids. Do not collapse a multi-participant process into a single flat pool.\n- Sequence flows must NEVER cross pool boundaries. Model every hand-over between pools as:\n  message END event in the sending pool -> message_flow -> message START event in the receiving pool.\n- Set trigger_type=\"message\" on those events and give the message a short message_name.\n- Only use a single pool (pools=[]) if the whole process is genuinely performed by one unit.\n\nEvents:\n- event_position is \"start\", \"intermediate\", or \"end\". Use \"intermediate\" for milestones inside a pool (e.g. a phase completed).\n- Use trigger_type=\"message\" only for events that send/receive something across pools.\n\nData perspective (IMPORTANT - do not skip):\n- data_objects: physical or informational ARTEFACTS that flow through the process - documents, drawings, programs, forms, part/tool lists, orders, reports, records, files. Extract every such artefact the text mentions.\n- data_stores: persistent information SYSTEMS or repositories in which data/status is recorded or from which it is retrieved - e.g. MES, ERP, CRM, program server, database, registry, archive, file store. Extract every such system the text mentions.\n- Connect them to tasks: if a task records/writes/updates a system or produces a document, put that data element id into the task's output_data_ids; if it reads/retrieves/uses one, into input_data_ids. Prefer to connect every data element to at least one task.\n- A system that only stores or serves data is a data_store, NOT a resource. Only list it as a resource if it actively performs work.\n\nTask types:\n- Use bpmn:ManualTask for physical work performed by hand, bpmn:ServiceTask for fully automated system actions, bpmn:UserTask for human work done in a software system, and bpmn:Task when unclear.\n- If the text states that a task repeats until a condition is met, set is_loop=true.\n\nReturn the complete ProcessModel as structured output."}, {"role": "human", "content": "Mail from the party is collected on a daily basis by the Mail Processing Unit. Within this unit, the Mail Clerk sorts the unopened mail into the various business areas. The mail is then distributed. When the mail is received by the Registry, it is opened and sorted into groups for distribution, and thus registered in a manual incoming Mail Register. Afterwards, the Assistant Registry Manager within the Registry performs a quality check. If the mail is not compliant, a list of requisition explaining the reason for rejection is compiled and sent back to the party. Otherwise, the matter details (types of action) are captured and provided to the Cashier, who takes the applicable fees attached to the mail. At this point, the Assistant Registry Manager puts the receipt and copied documents into an envelope and posts it to the party. Meantime, the Cashier captures the Party Details and prints the Physical Court File."}]}, "finished": "2026-10-02T09:58:20.593+00:00", "latency_s": 23.498, "outcome": "ok", "error": null, "model_returned": "claude-sonnet-5", "finish_reason": "tool_use", "input_tokens": 4432, "output_tokens": 3737, "response": {"content": [{"id": "toolu_01Cfai6JXh92bbKGYj1hxErU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"name": "Mail Processing and Registry Workflow", "pools": [{"id": "pool_mpu", "name": "Mail Processing Unit", "element_ids": ["start_mail_collected", "task_sort_unopened_mail", "end_mail_distributed"]}, {"id": "pool_registry", "name": "Registry", "element_ids": ["start_mail_received", "task_open_sort_register", "task_quality_check", "gw_compliant", "task_compile_requisition_list", "end_send_requisition", "task_capture_matter_details", "end_send_to_cashier", "start_receipt_from_cashier", "task_post_receipt", "end_registry_process"]}, {"id": "pool_cashier", "name": "Cashier", "element_ids": ["start_receive_matter_details", "task_take_fees", "task_capture_party_details", "task_print_physical_court_file", "end_send_receipt_to_registry"]}], "events": [{"id": "start_mail_collected", "name": "Mail collected from party", "event_position": "start"}, {"id": "end_mail_distributed", "name": "Mail distributed", "event_position": "end", "trigger_type": "message", "message_name": "Unopened Mail"}, {"id": "start_mail_received", "name": "Mail received at Registry", "event_position": "start", "trigger_type": "message", "message_name": "Unopened Mail"}, {"id": "end_send_requisition", "name": "Requisition list sent to party", "event_position": "end"}, {"id": "end_send_to_cashier", "name": "Matter details sent to Cashier", "event_position": "end", "trigger_type": "message", "message_name": "Matter Details"}, {"id": "start_receive_matter_details", "name": "Matter details received", "event_position": "start", "trigger_type": "message", "message_name": "Matter Details"}, {"id": "end_send_receipt_to_registry", "name": 